---
/** Privacy Policy -- noindexed via the page registry. */
import PageLayout from "@/layouts/PageLayout.astro";
import OwnerDetail from "@/components/content/OwnerDetail.astro";
import { SITE } from "@/config/site";
import { getPage } from "@/config/pages";

const contactPath = getPage("contact").path;
const disclosurePath = getPage("affiliate-disclosure").path;
---

<PageLayout pageId="privacy-policy" title="Privacy Policy" eyebrow="Legal">
  <p><strong>Effective date:</strong> 2 November 2026</p>

  <h2>Who we are</h2>
  <p>
    This privacy policy explains how {SITE.name} (&ldquo;we&rdquo;, &ldquo;us&rdquo;) handles
    information when you use this website. The site is operated by <OwnerDetail field="name" />.
    You can contact us about privacy at <OwnerDetail field="contactEmail" /> or through our
    <a href={contactPath}>contact page</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Information we collect</h2>
  <h3>Information you give us</h3>
  <p>
    When you use our contact form, we receive the name, email address, subject, and message you
    submit.
  </p>
  <p>
    When you subscribe to our email updates, the address you type is sent to our email provider,
    which stores it on the mailing list and sends the emails. We do not store subscriber addresses
    on this website, and we use an address given this way only to send those updates. Every email
    carries an unsubscribe link, and unsubscribing removes the address from the list.
  </p>
  <h3>Information collected automatically</h3>
  <p>
    Our hosting provider may process technical information needed to deliver the site, such as your
    IP address, browser type, and the pages you request.
  </p>
  <p>
    We use Google Analytics 4 (GA4) to understand how the site is used &mdash; which pages are
    visited, how long visits last, and where visitors come from. GA4 collects data such as your IP
    address (which Google anonymises), browser type, device type, pages viewed, and approximate
    location. This data is processed by Google under its own privacy policy. You can opt out by
    installing the{" "}
    <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout">Google Analytics Opt-out Browser Add-on</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>How we use information</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>To reply to messages sent through the contact form.</li>
    <li>To send our email updates to the people who have asked for them.</li>
    <li>To operate, secure, and maintain the website.</li>
    <li>To understand how the site is used so we can improve it.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    For visitors in the European Economic Area or United Kingdom, our legal basis for processing is:
    consent for email subscriptions and the contact form (you choose to submit your information),
    and legitimate interest for analytics (understanding site usage to improve it).
  </p>

  <h2>Cookies</h2>
  <p>This site uses the following cookies:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Google Analytics</strong> (<code>_ga</code>, <code>_ga_*</code>): used to distinguish
      visitors and track page views. These are set by the GA4 script and expire after 2 years
      (<code>_ga</code>) or 2 years (<code>_ga_*</code>).
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>hCaptcha</strong>: may set cookies when you use the contact form to verify you are not
      a bot. These are set by hCaptcha and are subject to their privacy policy.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    You can manage or block cookies through your browser settings. Blocking analytics cookies does
    not affect how the site works &mdash; you can still read every page and use every tool.
  </p>

  <h2>Third-party services</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Cloudflare</strong> hosts and serves the website.{" "}
      <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/">Cloudflare Privacy Policy</a>.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Web3Forms</strong> receives contact form submissions and emails them to us. The name,
      email address, subject, and message you type are sent to Web3Forms when you submit the form.{" "}
      <a href="https://web3forms.com/privacy">Web3Forms Privacy Policy</a>.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Kit (formerly ConvertKit)</strong> receives and stores the address you enter in the
      subscribe form, and sends the emails you have asked for. The form submits directly to them,
      so the address reaches them without passing through this website.{" "}
      <a href="https://kit.com/privacy">Kit Privacy Policy</a>.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>hCaptcha</strong> provides the anti-spam check on the contact form, through Web3Forms.
      Loading and completing that check sends your IP address and information about your browser and
      interaction with the page to hCaptcha, and may set cookies in your browser. It runs only on
      the contact page.{" "}
      <a href="https://www.hcaptcha.com/privacy">hCaptcha Privacy Policy</a>.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Google Analytics</strong> collects anonymous usage data as described above.{" "}
      <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">Google Privacy Policy</a>.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Affiliate partners:</strong> when you click an affiliate link, the partner may use
      cookies to attribute a purchase. See our <a href={disclosurePath}>affiliate disclosure</a>.
      We currently have no active affiliate partnerships. This section will be updated when we join
      any affiliate programs.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Advertising:</strong> we do not currently display advertising on this site. If we add
      advertising in the future, this section will be updated with the ad networks used and how they
      collect data.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>These services handle data under their own privacy policies, linked above.</p>

  <h2>How long we keep information</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Contact form submissions:</strong> we keep messages sent through the contact form for
      as long as needed to respond and resolve any follow-up, then delete them. We do not keep a
      permanent archive of contact messages.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Email subscriptions:</strong> your email address is stored by Kit for as long as you
      remain subscribed. Unsubscribing removes your address from the list.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Analytics data:</strong> Google Analytics retains data according to its own retention
      settings, which we have set to 14 months.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    Depending on where you live, you may have rights over your personal information, such as the
    right to access, correct, delete, or restrict the use of it, to object to processing, or to opt
    out of the sale or sharing of personal information. To make a request, contact us using the
    details above.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>European Economic Area and United Kingdom:</strong> under the GDPR and UK GDPR, you have
    the right to access, rectify, erase, restrict, or port your data, and to withdraw consent or
    object to processing. Contact us to exercise any of these rights. If you are not satisfied with
    our response, you have the right to lodge a complaint with your local data protection authority.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>California:</strong> under the CCPA/CPRA, you have the right to know what personal
    information we collect and how it is used, to request deletion, and to opt out of the sale or
    sharing of personal information. We do not sell or share personal information as defined by these
    laws.
  </p>

  <h2>Children&apos;s privacy</h2>
  <p>
    This website is not directed at children, and we do not knowingly collect their information.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>
    We may update this policy from time to time. The effective date at the top of this page shows
    when it was last changed.
  </p>
</PageLayout>
